    {
      "id": "l1",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Time, risk, stress",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Time, risk, stress"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/1-czas-ryzyko-stres.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Investing** – you buy with years in mind",
                "**Speculation (trading)** – you try to profit from price moves within days, hours or even minutes"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The shorter the time, the bigger the role of **chance** and the smaller the role of the company's value."
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "Trading needs constant attention and stress resistance – **one mistake** can cost a lot."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l2",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Fundamental vs technical analysis",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Fundamental vs technical analysis"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/2-analiza-fundamentalna-vs-tec.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Fundamental** – what the company is really worth: profits, debt, growth. It answers “**what** to buy”",
                "**Technical** – price chart and volume, patterns and trends. It answers “**when** to buy”"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Long-term investors look mostly at **fundamentals**, traders more often at **charts**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l3",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Why do most traders lose?",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Why do most traders lose?"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/3-dlaczego-traderzy-traca.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Main reasons:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Costs** – commissions, spread and taxes on every trade",
                "**Emotions** – holding on to losses and closing gains too early",
                "**Competition** – professionals and algorithms with better data"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "In the EU, CFD brokers must show what % of accounts lose money – usually it's **most clients**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l4",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "FOMO",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "FOMO"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/4-fomo.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**FOMO** (fear of missing out) is the fear of missing an opportunity because “everyone is making money”. It ends with buying after a big rise – often **right at the top**."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If everyone on social media is talking about something, the best moment has **usually already passed**."
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "The cure: **your own plan** and a rule that you never buy in a hurry."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
